  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the OpenSocrates guidance and the project files, then update the plan and the scoped continuity records. I’ll verify both the artifact and the persisted memory state afterward.",
    "The venue list now gives Cedar 48 seats, below the 52 attendees. Harbor has 65 seats and meets the listed access, quiet room, and budget requirements. I’ll update the plan to Harbor and check the continuity records before removing the withdrawn capacity fact.",
    "The plan now points to Harbor. The project notes retain the accepted workshop requirements and badge choice, while keeping the Birch idea explicitly proposed. I’m creating an accepted replacement for the mixed memory record before deleting that exact old record.",
    "Updated [plan.json](<disposable>/workspace/plan.json) to propose Harbor for 52 attendees: 65 seats, step-free entry, a quiet room, and a $1,300 cost within the $1,400 budget. No booking was made.\n\nUpdated [notes.md](<disposable>/workspace/notes.md) and the structured memory. The retained workshop intent is accepted; the old mixed record containing Cedar’s withdrawn 60-seat fact was deleted. I verified the persisted records: the blue badge decision remains accepted, and the Birch suggestion remains proposed. The plan and notes passed checks against the current venue source.\n\nOpenSocrates native activation was unconfirmed."
